/-!
# The converse of the Abel–Ruffini theorem

Mathlib's `Mathlib/FieldTheory/AbelRuffini.lean` proves that an irreducible polynomial with a root
in `solvableByRad F E` has a solvable Galois group. This file proves the converse in
characteristic zero: a finite Galois extension `E / F` has solvable Galois group exactly when,
under an `F`-embedding of `E` into an algebraic closure `Ω` of `F`, every element of `E` lands in
the radical closure `solvableByRad F Ω`; and a polynomial over `F` has solvable Galois group
exactly when all of its roots in `Ω` lie in `solvableByRad F Ω`.

The radical closure has to be taken in `Ω` rather than in `E`: the radicals that express the
elements of `E` may need roots of unity that are not in `E`. For the cyclic cubic field `E` of
`X ^ 3 - 3 * X + 1` over `ℚ`, `solvableByRad ℚ E` is `⊥`, although the group is solvable.

## Main results

* `solvableByRad.map_le_of_algHom`: a field embedding maps radicals to radicals.
* `solvableByRad.restrictScalars_eq`: if `K` consists of radicals over `F`, then the radicals over
  `K` are exactly the radicals over `F`.
* `IsPrimitiveRoot.isSeparable_of_finrank_dvd`: an extension `L / K` is separable if some
  extension of `K` contains a primitive `n`-th root of unity with `[L : K] ∣ n`.
* `TauCeti.solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isSolvable`: a normal extension `L / K` with solvable group is
  generated by radicals when `K` contains a primitive `n`-th root of unity with `[L : K] ∣ n`.
* `AlgHom.fieldRange_le_solvableByRad`: if `E / F` is normal with solvable group, then every
  embedding of `E` into a field containing a primitive `n`-th root of unity, with `[E : F] ∣ n`,
  lands in the radicals over `F`.
* `TauCeti.isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad`: the radical criterion for finite Galois
  extensions in characteristic zero.
* `TauCeti.isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad`: the radical criterion for
  polynomials in characteristic zero.
* `Irreducible.forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad`: in characteristic zero, if one root of an
  irreducible polynomial is expressible by radicals, then so are all of its roots.

## Implementation notes

The solvable-to-radical direction follows the classical argument. If `L / K` is finite normal with
solvable group and `K` contains a primitive `n`-th root of unity for a multiple `n` of `[L : K]`,
then `L / K` is separable, since the characteristic does not divide `n`, and `L` is generated by
radicals over `K`: otherwise `L` is a nontrivial solvable Galois extension of
`S = solvableByRad K L`, so it contains a cyclic extension `M / S` of prime degree `p`; by Kummer
theory `M = S(α)` with `α ^ p ∈ S`, which forces `α ∈ S` and `M = S`. For a finite normal `E / F`
with `[E : F] = n`, this applies to the compositum of the image of `E` with `F(ζ)` over `F(ζ)`,
for a primitive `n`-th root of unity `ζ`, whose Galois group embeds in that of `E / F`.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Fields and Galois Theory*, version 5.10 (2022), Theorem 5.34.
-/

public section

open Module IntermediateField Polynomial

section solvableByRad

variable {F E : Type*} [Field F] [Field E] [Algebra F E]

/-- An `F`-embedding maps elements solvable by radicals over `F` to elements solvable by radicals
over `F`. -/
theorem solvableByRad.map_le_of_algHom {K : Type*} [Field K] [Algebra F K] (i : E →ₐ[F] K) :
    (solvableByRad F E).map i ≤ solvableByRad F K := by
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  induction hx using solvableByRad.induction with
  | mem y => simp
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => simpa using add_mem hy hz
  | mul y z _ _ hy hz => simpa using mul_mem hy hz
  | rad n y hn _ hy => exact solvableByRad.rad_mem hn (by simpa using hy)

/-- If every element of an intermediate field `K` of `E / F` is solvable by radicals over `F`,
then the elements of `E` solvable by radicals over `K` are exactly those solvable by radicals over
`F`. -/
theorem solvableByRad.restrictScalars_eq {K : Type*} [Field K] [Algebra F K] [Algebra K E]
    [IsScalarTower F K E] (h : ∀ x : K, algebraMap K E x ∈ solvableByRad F E) :
    (solvableByRad K E).restrictScalars F = solvableByRad F E := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx ↦ ?_) (solvableByRad_le fun x n hn hx ↦
    (mem_restrictScalars F).2 (solvableByRad.rad_mem hn ((mem_restrictScalars F).1 hx)))
  rw [mem_restrictScalars] at hx
  induction hx using solvableByRad.induction with
  | mem y => exact h y
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => exact add_mem hy hz
  | mul y z _ _ hy hz => exact mul_mem hy hz
  | rad n y hn _ hy => exact solvableByRad.rad_mem hn hy

end solvableByRad

/-- An extension `L / K` is separable if some extension `Ω` of `K` contains a primitive `n`-th root
of unity for some `n ≠ 0` divisible by `[L : K]`: then `n ≠ 0` in `K`, hence so is `[L : K]`. -/
theorem IsPrimitiveRoot.isSeparable_of_finrank_dvd {K L Ω : Type*} [Field K] [Field L] [Field Ω]
    [Algebra K L] [Algebra K Ω] {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] {ζ : Ω} (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n)
    (hn : finrank K L ∣ n) : Algebra.IsSeparable K L := by
  have := hζ.neZero'
  refine TauCeti.Algebra.isSeparable_of_cast_finrank_ne_zero fun h ↦ NeZero.ne (n : Ω) ?_
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := hn
  rw [Nat.cast_mul, ← map_natCast (algebraMap K Ω), h, map_zero, zero_mul]

namespace TauCeti

/-- **Solvable normal extensions are radical.** Let `L / K` be a normal extension with solvable
group, and suppose `K` contains a primitive `n`-th root of unity for some `n ≠ 0` divisible by
`[L : K]`. Then every element of `L` is solvable by radicals over `K`. -/
theorem solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isSolvable {K L : Type*} [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra K L]
    [Normal K L] [Group.IsSolvable Gal(L/K)] {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] {ζ : K}
    (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n) (hn : finrank K L ∣ n) : solvableByRad K L = ⊤ := by
  have : IsGalois K L := { to_isSeparable := hζ.isSeparable_of_finrank_dvd hn }
  have : FiniteDimensional K L :=
    Module.finite_of_finrank_pos (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero fun h ↦ NeZero.ne n (zero_dvd_iff.1 (h ▸ hn)))
  set S := solvableByRad K L
  by_contra hS
  -- `Gal(L/S)` is a nontrivial solvable group, so it has a normal subgroup `N` of prime index `p`.
  have : Group.IsSolvable Gal(L/S) := (fixingSubgroupEquiv S).isSolvable_congr.mp inferInstance
  have : Nontrivial Gal(L/S) := by
    rw [← Finite.one_lt_card_iff_nontrivial, IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank]
    have := finrank_eq_one_iff_eq_top.not.mpr hS
    have := finrank_pos (R := S) (M := L)
    omega
  obtain ⟨N, hN, hp⟩ := Group.IsSolvable.exists_normal_index_prime Gal(L/S)
  -- The fixed field `M` of `N` is a cyclic extension of `S` of degree `p`.
  let M := fixedField N
  have hM : finrank S M = N.index := by
    rw [finrank_eq_fixingSubgroup_index, fixingSubgroup_fixedField]
  have : IsGalois S M := IsGalois.of_fixedField_normal_subgroup N
  have : Fact N.index.Prime := ⟨hp⟩
  have : IsCyclic Gal(M/S) :=
    isCyclic_of_prime_card (p := N.index) (by rw [IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank, hM])
  -- `S` contains a primitive `p`-th root of unity, since `p ∣ [L : K] ∣ n`.
  have hpn : N.index ∣ n :=
    N.index_dvd_card.trans <| (IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank S L).dvd.trans <|
      (Dvd.intro_left _ (finrank_mul_finrank K S L)).trans hn
  have hroot : (primitiveRoots (finrank S M) S).Nonempty := by
    rw [hM]
    have h := hζ.pow_of_dvd (Nat.div_ne_zero_iff_of_dvd hpn |>.2 ⟨NeZero.ne n, hp.ne_zero⟩)
      (Nat.div_dvd_of_dvd hpn)
    rw [Nat.div_div_self hpn (NeZero.ne n)] at h
    exact ⟨_, (mem_primitiveRoots hp.pos).2 (h.map_of_injective (algebraMap K S).injective)⟩
  -- By Kummer theory `M = S(α)` with `α ^ p ∈ S`; then `α` is a radical, so `M = S`.
  obtain ⟨α, ⟨a, ha⟩, hα⟩ := exists_root_adjoin_eq_top_of_isCyclic S M hroot
  have hpow : (α : L) ^ finrank S M = a := by
    rw [← SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, ← ha, coe_algebraMap_apply, IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply]
  have hαS : (α : L) ∈ S := solvableByRad.rad_mem finrank_pos.ne' (hpow ▸ a.property)
  have hbot : S⟮α⟯ = ⊥ := adjoin_simple_eq_bot_iff.2 (mem_bot.2 ⟨⟨α, hαS⟩, Subtype.ext (by simp)⟩)
  rw [hα, eq_comm, bot_eq_top_iff_finrank_eq_one, hM] at hbot
  exact hp.ne_one hbot

/-- **Solvable normal extensions embed into radicals.** Let `E / F` be a normal extension with
solvable group, and let `ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω` be an embedding into a field `Ω` that contains a primitive
`n`-th root of unity for some `n ≠ 0` divisible by `[E : F]`. Then the image of `ι` consists of
elements of `Ω` solvable by radicals over `F`. -/
theorem _root_.AlgHom.fieldRange_le_solvableByRad {F E Ω : Type*} [Field F] [Field E] [Field Ω]
    [Algebra F E] [Algebra F Ω] [Normal F E] [Group.IsSolvable Gal(E/F)] (ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω)
    {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] {ζ : Ω} (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n) (hn : finrank F E ∣ n) :
    ι.fieldRange ≤ solvableByRad F Ω := by
  have : IsGalois F E := { to_isSeparable := hζ.isSeparable_of_finrank_dvd hn }
  have : FiniteDimensional F E :=
    Module.finite_of_finrank_pos (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero fun h ↦ NeZero.ne n (zero_dvd_iff.1 (h ▸ hn)))
  -- Inside the compositum `C` of `ι(E)` and `F(ζ)`, the copies `A` of `ι(E)` and `B` of `F(ζ)`
  -- generate `C`, and `C / B` is Galois with group embedding into `Gal(A/F) ≃ Gal(E/F)`.
  let C := ι.fieldRange ⊔ F⟮ζ⟯
  let A : IntermediateField F C := restrict (le_sup_left : ι.fieldRange ≤ C)
  let B : IntermediateField F C := restrict (le_sup_right : F⟮ζ⟯ ≤ C)
  have hAB : A ⊔ B = ⊤ := lift_injective _ <| by simp [A, B, C, lift_sup, lift_restrict, lift_top]
  let eA : E ≃ₐ[F] A := ι.equivFieldRange.trans (restrictAlgEquiv _)
  have : IsGalois F A := IsGalois.of_algEquiv eA
  have : FiniteDimensional F A := eA.toLinearEquiv.finiteDimensional
  have : FiniteDimensional F ι.fieldRange := ι.equivFieldRange.toLinearEquiv.finiteDimensional
  have : FiniteDimensional F F⟮ζ⟯ :=
    adjoin.finiteDimensional ((hζ.isIntegral (NeZero.pos n)).tower_top (A := F))
  have : FiniteDimensional F C := finiteDimensional_sup _ _
  have : IsGalois B C := IsGalois.sup_right A B hAB
  have hφ := restrictRestrictAlgEquivMapHom_injective A B hAB
  have : Group.IsSolvable Gal(A/F) := eA.autCongr.isSolvable_congr.mp inferInstance
  have : Group.IsSolvable Gal(C/B) := Group.isSolvable_of_isSolvable_injective hφ
  have hBC : finrank B C ∣ n := by
    have h := Subgroup.card_dvd_of_injective _ hφ
    rw [IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank, IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank,
      ← eA.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq] at h
    exact h.trans hn
  -- `B` contains the primitive root `ζ`, so `C` is generated by radicals over `B`.
  have hζC : ζ ∈ C := (le_sup_right : F⟮ζ⟯ ≤ C) (mem_adjoin_simple_self F ζ)
  let ζB : B := ⟨⟨ζ, hζC⟩, (mem_restrict _ _).2 (mem_adjoin_simple_self F ζ)⟩
  have hζB : IsPrimitiveRoot ζB n :=
    .of_map_of_injective (f := C.val.comp B.val) (by simpa [ζB] using hζ)
      (C.val.comp B.val).injective
  have hradB : solvableByRad B C = ⊤ := solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isSolvable hζB hBC
  -- `F(ζ)` consists of radicals over `F`, hence so does `C`, and then so does `ι(E)` in `Ω`.
  have hζn : (⟨ζ, hζC⟩ : C) ^ n = 1 := Subtype.ext (by simp [hζ.pow_eq_one])
  have hζR : (⟨ζ, hζC⟩ : C) ∈ solvableByRad F C :=
    solvableByRad.rad_mem (NeZero.ne n) (hζn ▸ one_mem _)
  have hB : ∀ y : B, algebraMap B C y ∈ solvableByRad F C := by
    have hle : F⟮ζ⟯ ≤ (solvableByRad F C).map C.val := adjoin_simple_le_iff.2 ⟨_, hζR, rfl⟩
    intro y
    obtain ⟨c, hc, hcy⟩ := hle ((mem_restrict _ _).1 y.property)
    have hcy' : c = y.val := Subtype.ext (by simpa using hcy)
    rw [IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply, ← hcy']
    exact hc
  have hC : solvableByRad F C = ⊤ := by
    rw [← solvableByRad.restrictScalars_eq hB, hradB, restrictScalars_top]
  intro x hx
  exact solvableByRad.map_le_of_algHom C.val
    ⟨⟨x, (le_sup_left : ι.fieldRange ≤ C) hx⟩, by rw [hC]; exact mem_top, rfl⟩

/-- **The radical criterion for finite Galois extensions** (Milne, *Fields and Galois Theory*,
Theorem 5.34). In characteristic zero, a finite Galois extension `E / F` has solvable Galois group
exactly when, under an `F`-embedding `ι` of `E` into an algebraic closure of `F`, every element of
`E` lands in the radical closure of `F` there. The radical closure is taken in the algebraic
closure, not in `E`. -/
theorem isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad (F E : Type*) [Field F] [CharZero F] [Field E]
    [Algebra F E] [FiniteDimensional F E] [IsGalois F E] (ι : E →ₐ[F] AlgebraicClosure F) :
    Group.IsSolvable (E ≃ₐ[F] E) ↔ ∀ x : E, ι x ∈ solvableByRad F (AlgebraicClosure F) := by
  refine ⟨fun _ ↦ ?_, fun h ↦ ?_⟩
  · have : NeZero (finrank F E) := ⟨finrank_pos.ne'⟩
    have : NeZero (finrank F E : F) := ⟨Nat.cast_ne_zero.2 finrank_pos.ne'⟩
    obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ :=
      HasEnoughRootsOfUnity.exists_isPrimitiveRoot (AlgebraicClosure F) (finrank F E)
    exact fun x ↦ ι.fieldRange_le_solvableByRad hζ dvd_rfl (AlgHom.mem_fieldRange.2 ⟨x, rfl⟩)
  · -- `E = F(α)` is the splitting field of `minpoly F α`, whose Galois group is solvable.
    obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := Field.exists_primitive_element F E
    have := isSplittingField_minpoly_of_adjoin_simple_eq_top α hα
    have h' := isSolvable_gal_minpoly (h α)
    rw [minpoly.algHom_eq ι ι.injective] at h'
    exact (IsSplittingField.algEquiv E (minpoly F α)).autCongr.isSolvable_congr.mpr h'

/-- **The radical criterion for polynomials.** In characteristic zero, a polynomial has solvable
Galois group exactly when **every** one of its roots in an algebraic closure lies in the radical
closure of the base field. Reducible polynomials are included; for them one radical root does not
suffice, as `(X ^ 5 - 4 * X + 2) * (X - 1)` over `ℚ` shows. -/
theorem isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad (F : Type*) [Field F] [CharZero F]
    (q : F[X]) :
    Group.IsSolvable q.Gal ↔
      ∀ x ∈ q.rootSet (AlgebraicClosure F), x ∈ solvableByRad F (AlgebraicClosure F) := by
  have : IsGalois F q.SplittingField := {}
  let ι : q.SplittingField →ₐ[F] AlgebraicClosure F := IsAlgClosed.lift
  have hroots : ι '' q.rootSet q.SplittingField = q.rootSet (AlgebraicClosure F) :=
    (SplittingField.splits q).image_rootSet ι
  refine (isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad F q.SplittingField ι).trans
    ⟨fun h x hx ↦ ?_, fun h x ↦ ?_⟩
  · rw [← hroots] at hx
    obtain ⟨y, -, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact h y
  · -- The roots of `q` generate its splitting field, and they all map into the radicals.
    have : Algebra.adjoin F (q.rootSet q.SplittingField) ≤
        (solvableByRad F (AlgebraicClosure F)).toSubalgebra.comap ι :=
      Algebra.adjoin_le fun y hy ↦ by simpa using h (ι y) (hroots ▸ Set.mem_image_of_mem ι hy)
    rw [SplittingField.adjoin_rootSet] at this
    simpa using this Algebra.mem_top

/-- In characteristic zero, if one root of an irreducible polynomial in an algebraic closure is
expressible by radicals, then so are all of its roots. -/
theorem _root_.Irreducible.forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad {F : Type*} [Field F] [CharZero F]
    {q : F[X]} (hq : Irreducible q) {x : AlgebraicClosure F} (hx : aeval x q = 0)
    (hxR : x ∈ solvableByRad F (AlgebraicClosure F)) :
    ∀ y ∈ q.rootSet (AlgebraicClosure F), y ∈ solvableByRad F (AlgebraicClosure F) :=
  (isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad F q).mp
    (isSolvable_gal_of_irreducible hxR hq hx)

end TauCeti
